**Calibration.** On the local replay (bench-keyed LOBO draws of matharena, multi_swebench, real_webagents, researchcodebench, k = 1, 2, 216 pair-draws per model, pair-equal weights, 10 equal-mass bins), the ECE of W20+SCP is 0.1180 at B0 and 0.0295 at B31 against 0.1492 and 0.0327 for base (REF) (ALC-weighted 0.0392 against 0.0578). In the binned Murphy decomposition (Brier = REL - RES + UNC + R, UNC = 232.01 x 1e-3 for every model and budget), the ALC difference of -3.10 ± 0.65 x 1e-3 splits into REL -2.70 ± 0.76, RES +0.61 ± 0.50 (a RES increase lowers Brier) and within-bin terms +0.21 ± 0.24 (draw-clustered bootstrap SEs). The platform-style ECE (ten fixed bins within each pair, ALC-weighted, mean over pairs; the leaderboard's diagnostic) is 0.1349 for W20+SCP and 0.1383 for base (REF); with 44 to 113 evaluation items per pair it is dominated by within-pair binning noise: a perfectly calibrated forecaster with the same predictions would score 0.0483 (pooled ECE floor 0.0084).

